    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"joy\" is just a temporary chemical spike in the brain. once the spike ends, you're back to zero. if the end result of every life is just zero, then the math doesn't really add up for why we should bother struggling just to stay at zero. it's like spending all your energy to maintain a sum that eventually cancels itself out.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
