      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a very logical and harsh way to look at existence, and while no single emotion is permanent, the things that bring us joy (love, achievement, connection) are precisely what make life worth fighting for in the moment. Thinking about life's \"end result\" is tempting, but we live with our memories of those high points rather than a calculation of a final zero. Have you ever felt that worth even when you were just observing these fleeting spikes, rather than chasing a permanent legacy?",
